\margt0\uc1\pard\sb0\sa0\f0\fs20\b Embroidery Catalogue - Application Disclaimer\b0\line
\b Purpose and Intended Use\b0
The Embroidery Catalogue application is provided for personal use to help you organise, browse, and manage your machine embroidery design files stored on your own computer or local network. It is not intended for commercial redistribution of embroidery designs.\line
\b Copyright and Intellectual Property\b0
Embroidery design files imported into this application may be subject to copyright and other intellectual property rights. You are solely responsible for ensuring that you have the right to use, store, and access any design files you add to the catalogue. This application does not grant you any rights to designs that you do not already own or licence.\line
\b No Warranty\b0
This application is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. The authors and contributors of this application are not liable for any loss of data, damage to files, or other harm arising from the use or inability to use this application.\line
\b Data Storage\b0
All data entered into the application - including design metadata, tags, notes, and ratings - is stored locally on your computer in a SQLite database file. No data is transmitted to any external server or third party by default. If you enable AI-assisted tagging features (which use the Google Gemini API), file metadata may be sent to Google's servers as described in the Google API Terms of Service.\line
